WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.647
A robots.txt file tells search engine robots which parts of your site they may visit.

00:00:06.647 --> 00:00:09.688
Orchard Core builds the file from settings.

00:00:09.688 --> 00:00:14.466
In this video, you'll enable the SEO feature, see the default file, and

00:00:14.466 --> 00:00:17.010
change it from the Robots settings.

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:27.123
Search engines send programs, called web robots or crawlers, to visit your pages.

00:00:27.123 --> 00:00:32.065
A robots.txt file at the root of your site gives those robots directives

00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:35.360
about which parts of the site they may access.

00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:38.511
Orchard Core can generate this file.

00:00:38.511 --> 00:00:43.543
The SEO feature provides the Robots settings, which decide what the file contains,

00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:45.830
so you do not edit a file by hand.

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:49.035
The Robots settings have three parts:

00:00:49.035 --> 00:00:53.088
a rule that addresses all robots, a rule that asks robots to stay

00:00:53.088 --> 00:00:56.970
out of the admin pages, and a text area for rules of your own.

00:01:01.267 --> 00:01:04.618
The Robots settings belong to the SEO feature.

00:01:04.618 --> 00:01:08.807
Let's open Tools, Features, and type SEO in the search box.

00:01:09.281 --> 00:01:12.009
SEO is listed under Content Management.

00:01:12.009 --> 00:01:17.039
Let's select Enable, and a message confirms that the SEO feature was enabled.

00:01:17.039 --> 00:01:23.341
The same feature also provides SEO meta features for content items, which a separate video covers.

00:01:27.602 --> 00:01:33.172
With the feature enabled, the site serves a robots.txt file at its root.

00:01:33.172 --> 00:01:36.242
Let's open robots.txt in the browser.

00:01:36.742 --> 00:01:38.622
The file holds two lines.

00:01:38.622 --> 00:01:44.384
The first addresses every robot, and the second asks robots not to visit the admin pages.

00:01:44.384 --> 00:01:47.902
These are the default values of the Robots settings.

00:01:52.139 --> 00:01:56.885
Let's open Settings, Search, Search Engine Optimization, and then Robots.

00:01:56.885 --> 00:01:59.889
The page has two checkboxes and a text area.

00:02:00.359 --> 00:02:04.468
The first checkbox, Add a rule to allow all web robots, adds the

00:02:04.468 --> 00:02:06.170
line shown in its hint.

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:07.989
It is checked by default.

00:02:08.449 --> 00:02:12.353
The second checkbox, Add a rule to disallow web robots to the admin

00:02:12.353 --> 00:02:15.562
routes, adds the line in its hint for your admin path.

00:02:15.562 --> 00:02:19.252
It is checked by default too, and a cleared box leaves its line

00:02:19.252 --> 00:02:20.429
out of the file.

00:02:21.009 --> 00:02:25.494
Additional rules is a text area for any other lines you want in the file.

00:02:25.494 --> 00:02:30.319
Let's type a rule that asks robots to skip a section of the site called drafts.

00:02:30.816 --> 00:02:32.276
Let's select Save.

00:02:32.276 --> 00:02:36.836
The message, Site settings updated successfully, confirms the change.

00:02:37.297 --> 00:02:39.499
Let's open robots.txt again.

00:02:39.499 --> 00:02:42.866
Your rule appears after the two default lines.

00:02:42.866 --> 00:02:46.947
The file is public, so anyone can read the rules you add.

00:02:51.147 --> 00:02:55.739
When the Sitemaps feature is enabled too, the Robots page also shows a

00:02:55.739 --> 00:02:58.276
checkbox named Include all sitemaps.

00:02:58.276 --> 00:03:01.177
A separate video covers creating sitemaps.

00:03:01.927 --> 00:03:06.711
After you save, and while Include all sitemaps is checked, Sitemap lines list

00:03:06.711 --> 00:03:11.438
your enabled sitemap indexes and any enabled sitemap that is not inside one.

00:03:11.438 --> 00:03:15.531
The lines are built from the Base url in the General settings, so

00:03:15.531 --> 00:03:16.857
fill it in first.

00:03:17.607 --> 00:03:21.909
If the static files of your site already include a robots.txt file, the

00:03:21.909 --> 00:03:25.095
site serves that file instead of the generated one.

00:03:25.095 --> 00:03:29.230
The Robots page can then show a warning that the settings below have

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:31.577
no effect until the file is removed.

00:03:33.577 --> 00:03:37.458
The Robots settings let you decide what search engines are asked to crawl,

00:03:37.458 --> 00:03:38.865
without editing a file.

00:03:38.865 --> 00:03:40.127
Thanks for watching.

